---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro"
---

<Layout
  title="The Builder — Scudra"
  description="An agent writes an application, boots it inside a sandbox with a live preview URL, then destroys it. Prompt. Boot. Build. Vanish."
>
  <article class="sc-container py-20 max-w-[72ch]" data-reveal>
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-muted mb-4">
      <a href="/experiences" class="no-underline text-inherit hover:text-ink">← Experiences</a>
    </p>

    <h1 class="font-serif text-[clamp(2.25rem,5vw,3.5rem)] leading-[1.1] tracking-tight mb-4">
      The Builder
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">
      Prompt. Boot. Build. Vanish. The Builder plans a small app from a prompt, writes it as a self-contained HTML file, boots it inside a fresh sandbox, and exposes a live preview URL. One minute later, the sandbox is destroyed — and the URL becomes a tombstone.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-12">
      <a
        href="https://github.com/scudra/scudra/tree/main/apps/builder"
        class="sc-button-primary"
      >
        Run it locally
      </a>
      <a
        href="/recipes/the-builder"
        class="sc-button-secondary"
      >
        Read the recipe
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 bg-paper-warm rounded-sc border border-black/5">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-4">What it demonstrates</h2>
      <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
        <li><strong>Software born on stage.</strong> Plan → write → boot → preview, streamed live over SSE.</li>
        <li><strong>Port preview.</strong> A server running inside the VM is exposed on the public internet at a <code>*.preview</code> URL the visitor can click.</li>
        <li><strong>Guaranteed teardown.</strong> The sandbox is destroyed on every path — success, failure, or timeout.</li>
        <li><strong>The tombstone.</strong> The finale invites you to revisit the URL after the kill and watch it fail. You were never there.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
